    "done_when": "imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py names each type-6 entry FL<L>-FL7 (FL1-FL7 ... FL27-FL7) in place of FL7-FL<L>, because the entry stores psi_L - psi_7 under indices_differential [7, L]. The type-6 entries keep their order, indices_differential, values and every other field. The OP1 and OP2 stores under /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/machine_description are regenerated with the merged build_magnetics. Their current magnetics.nc and receipt.json are copied first to /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/superseded/differential-loop-names-pre-rename/OP1 and OP2. A script logged in the run directory shows every array in the regenerated stores equal to the pre-rename stores except the type-6 names. The per-entry bindings in /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/machine_map.json select the renamed entries; they are regenerated with an adapted copy of /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/maps-staging/jtmm-differential-loop-consumers/build_staged_flux_loop_bindings.py kept in the run directory, not hand-edited, and binding ids carrying the old pair are renamed to match. The prior machine_map.json goes into the same superseded directory. The fragment records sha256s before and after for every changed bundle file. tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py and tests/data/test_selene_deck.py pin the new names, with a test asserting a type-6 entry named FL<L>-FL7 carries indices_differential [7, L]. maps/jt-60sa/maps/magnetics.json is untouched, since its rules target by index. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset and the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground with a time bound and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_selene_deck.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/gs/test_operator.py tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_unit_audit.py. It exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Write the manifest before any long wait. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
